  "objective_results": "X-ray of the right elbow - No acute fracture or other bony abnormality; no malalignment or sign of joint effusion; normal right elbow x-ray.",
  "assessment_and_plan": "ASSESSMENT AND PLAN: Acute lateral epicondylitis (tennis elbow) - Rest arm for 4-6 weeks, avoid repetitive stress, ice right elbow for 20 minutes at least three times per day, prescribe Ultram (50 mg once daily), follow-up in four weeks.\nDiabetes type 2 - Increase metformin to 1000 mg twice daily, check blood sugar twice daily for two weeks, order hemoglobin A1c and CBC blood tests.\nMild intermittent asthma - Continue Flovent and Albuterol as tolerated; write prescription refill for Albuterol."
}

